From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] util/disk_cache: keep the shader disk cache on by default on Android biblioklept

Upstream turns the Mesa disk cache off by default on Android because
the EGL layer brings its own blob cache. This build is a Vulkan-only
driver that mostly runs under Wine + DXVK, where nothing else caches
compiled shaders, so every session recompiled every pipeline.

It also hurts within a session: 32-bit DXVK compiles each shader
pipeline library on a worker, destroys it right away to save address
space ("we should hit the driver's disk cache"), and recreates it on
dxvk-cs at first draw. panvk's in-memory pipeline cache only holds weak
references, so without the disk cache that second create is a full
compile on the render thread (NFS Most Wanted: 0.65 s per pipeline,
1-1.6 s freezes).

Use the normal default. The path still comes from
$MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR, $XDG_CACHE_HOME or $HOME/.cache; when none of
them is writable (a plain Android app) path init fails and the cache
stays inert, as before. MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=true still turns it
off. The cache key already includes the driver BuildID and the GPU id.
---
diff --git a/src/util/disk_cache_os.c b/src/util/disk_cache_os.c
index 66a3f5b..08165bb 100644
--- a/src/util/disk_cache_os.c
+++ b/src/util/disk_cache_os.c
@@ -1007,14 +1007,13 @@ disk_cache_enabled()
       return false;
 
    /* At user request, disable shader cache entirely.
-    * Disk cache is not enabled by default for android, for most
-    * applications the EGL layer uses EGL_ANDROID_blob_cache to manage
-    * the cache itself, however those that wish to use the cache directly
-    * can set `mesa.shader.cache.disable=false` property.
-    * Don't forget to also set the shader cache path to something readable
-    * and writable by the application via `mesa.shader.cache.dir`.
+    * Upstream disables the disk cache by default on Android because the EGL
+    * layer manages its own blob cache. This build is a Vulkan-only driver
+    * that mostly runs under Wine/DXVK, where nothing else caches shaders:
+    * keep it on. Without a writable $MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR, $XDG_CACHE_HOME
+    * or $HOME/.cache the path init fails and the cache stays inert.
     */
-#if defined(SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE_BY_DEFAULT) || DETECT_OS_ANDROID
+#if defined(SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE_BY_DEFAULT)
    bool disable_by_default = true;
 #else
    bool disable_by_default = false;
